"},{"path":"storyscenes/mini_adventures/kite/reference_story.md","content":"# The Pears We Could Reach

On Tuesday morning, Mira packed two slices of bread in a cloth and found Theo waiting beside the lane. He had brought no food, but he had brought a careful list: basket, pears, home before the sun got hot. “You make a picnic sound like a delivery route,” Mira said. “I’m hungry in an organized way,” Theo replied. They were both hungry, and the little orchard at the end of the lane had the first ripe pears of the season.

The orchard belonged to Ms. Vale, who was sorting labels beside her shed. Mira asked if they could borrow the picking basket. Ms. Vale inspected its handles, then handed it over. “The basket is for carrying fruit, not for climbing. Bring it back clean, please.” Theo nodded before Mira could answer. They wanted a snack, not a scolding, and Mira liked that Ms. Vale trusted them with something useful.

At the orchard edge, Theo noticed a wooden crate. He pressed its corners against the ground. It sat level, so they spread their lunch cloth across it and made a little sorting table. “It would make a terrible ladder,” he said. Mira looked up at the pears. “I wasn’t going to climb it.” “I know,” he said, and moved it nearer the path. The crate could hold the bread while the basket stayed empty for fruit.

As they walked, Mira remembered the pear they had shared the previous summer. She had insisted Theo take the larger half because he was younger and still growing. “You said you were already tall enough,” Theo reminded her. “I was talking about my ideas,” she said. They laughed. This time she wanted the snack to feel like something they had made together, not a favor she had handed down.

The tree was older than both of them, with a thick trunk and branches that reached over the grass. Some pears were high, shining green-gold in the leaves. Others hung lower, but only a few. Theo studied the branches from the ground. Mira stretched one arm toward a low pear and could just touch it with her fingertips. A breeze moved the higher limbs. The fruit there looked plentiful, and farther away than it had from the lane.

Mira fetched the crate with her foot, then stopped before dragging it under the tree. One corner wobbled on the uneven grass. “If I stand on it, I can reach the big cluster,” she said. Theo looked at the rocking crate, then at the branch. “And if it tips, you fall. If you pull, the branch takes the strain.” He did not sound bossy. He sounded worried about the tree and about her. Mira let go of the crate.

They could have tried anyway. The biggest pears were just beyond a stretch, and the basket was waiting. Instead, Mira chose the lower fruit and the pear already resting on the grass. She checked the fallen one gently for bruises. Theo held the basket by its rim as Mira turned one reachable pear upward, the way Ms. Vale had shown them. The stem came away easily. No leaves tore, and no branch bent under their hands.

One pear was all they could gather without reaching or tugging. It looked small in the basket, but Mira put the bread beside it in the cloth. At the crate-table they cut the pear into two equal pieces with the little picnic knife Ms. Vale had loaned them with the basket. Theo offered Mira the larger piece. “We’ve already had this argument,” she said, and traded him half. They ate slowly, with the orchard moving softly around them.

When they were done, Theo folded the cloth and Mira checked that no crumbs had been left under the tree. She brushed a leaf from the basket and carried it back between them. At the shed, Ms. Vale ran her thumb over the clean weave. “Did it do its job?” she asked. “It carried our snack all the way here,” Mira said. Theo added, “And we left your tree whole.” Ms. Vale smiled as she took it.

On the walk home, Mira admitted she had wanted enough pears to make a grand picnic. Theo said he had wanted proof she would listen when he was worried. “I listened because you were right,” she said. “Not because you were in charge.” He considered this, then grinned. Their small snack was gone, but neither felt short-changed. They had chosen what the tree could spare, shared it fairly, and returned the basket ready for its next useful day."},{"path":"storyscenes/mini_adventures/kite/scene_inventory.json","content":"{"scenes":[{"id":"ask_ms_vale","role":"borrowed-object setup","location":"shed","prerequisites":["The friends arrive at Ms. Vale's shed."],"actions":["Ask to borrow the picking basket; accept the condition to return it clean."],"consequences":["The friends take responsibility for a useful borrowed object."],"prose_obligations":["Show Mira's ordinary desire for a pear snack and Ms. Vale's trust."],"implemented_ids":["borrow_basket"],"implementation_note":"Executable borrowing and orchard entry are combined into borrow_basket."},{"id":"carry_basket_into_orchard","role":"transition","location":"shed to orchard","prerequisites":["Ms. Vale lends the basket."],"actions":["Carry the empty basket into the orchard."],"consequences":["Basket and friends arrive together."],"prose_obligations":["Establish that the basket is for carrying, not climbing."],"implemented_ids":["borrow_basket"],"implementation_note":"Consolidated with the borrowing action; there is no separate travel scene."},{"id":"find_crate","role":"optional vignette","location":"orchard edge","prerequisites":["The friends have entered the orchard."],"actions":["Notice the wooden crate near the path."],"consequences":["The crate may provide a sorting surface."],"prose_obligations":["Treat the crate as an ordinary prop, not an automatic ladder."],"implemented_ids":["vignette_crate"],"implementation_note":"Combined with the crate stability test."},{"id":"test_crate","role":"optional vignette","location":"orchard edge","prerequisites":["The crate is available on the ground."],"actions":["Press its corners to see whether it sits level."],"consequences":["A level crate becomes a sorting table; an unstable one is left aside."],"prose_obligations":["Never invite a child to climb an unstable crate."],"implemented_ids":["vignette_crate"],"implementation_note":"Executable as one local play; it changes the picnic surface and crate state."},{"id":"remember_last_summer","role":"optional vignette","location":"orchard path","prerequisites":["Mira and Theo walk together."],"actions":["Recall sharing a pear the previous summer."],"consequences":["A shared memory can inform the later snack dialogue."],"prose_obligations":["Give the friends distinct voices and a history without making the memory mandatory."],"implemented_ids":["vignette_memory"],"implementation_note":"Optional, persistent memory flag; omitted routes do not receive the memory callback."},{"id":"walk_to_tree","role":"essential transition","location":"orchard","prerequisites":["The basket is borrowed."],"actions":["Walk from the orchard edge to the pear tree with the empty basket."],"consequences":["The party and basket arrive at the tree."],"prose_obligations":["Keep object and party location in step."],"implemented_ids":["survey_tree"],"implementation_note":"Combined with the ground-level survey."},{"id":"watch_the_leaves","role":"essential observation","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["The friends are beneath the tree."],"actions":["Observe whether the branches are moving."],"consequences":["Moving branches make reaching for fruit unsafe."],"prose_obligations":["State only what the characters can observe."],"implemented_ids":["survey_tree"],"implementation_note":"The wind parameter determines the local observation."},{"id":"check_reach","role":"essential observation","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["The friends survey from the ground."],"actions":["Check whether the lowest ripe cluster is comfortably reachable."],"consequences":["Reach and wind jointly determine a safe low-branch option."],"prose_obligations":["Do not smuggle in climbing or branch-pulling."],"implemented_ids":["survey_tree"],"implementation_note":"Consolidated with watching the leaves in survey_tree."},{"id":"admire_high_cluster","role":"complication","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["The survey reveals fruit beyond easy reach."],"actions":["Notice the tempting higher pears."],"consequences":["The friends must decide whether abundance is worth a risk."],"prose_obligations":["Make the temptation ordinary and understandable."],"implemented_ids":["choose_harvest"],"implementation_note":"The decision scene covers both safe low fruit and ground-only choices."},{"id":"consider_crate_as_step","role":"consequential choice","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["Some fruit is out of comfortable reach."],"actions":["Consider using the crate or tugging a limb; decline both."],"consequences":["The tree remains undamaged and no one climbs."],"prose_obligations":["Make restraint a choice, not an invisible rule."],"implemented_ids":["choose_harvest"],"implementation_note":"The reference encounter is consolidated with selecting a safe harvest plan; the executable never climbs."},{"id":"choose_low_or_ground","role":"consequential choice","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["The tree has been surveyed."],"actions":["Choose reachable low pears when safe, otherwise choose fallen fruit."],"consequences":["The selected harvest method changes what can be gathered."],"prose_obligations":["Let the smaller harvest be a complete, valued decision."],"implemented_ids":["choose_harvest"],"implementation_note":"The parameter-guarded local plan is executable."},{"id":"turn_low_pears","role":"harvest encounter","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["Low fruit is safely reachable."],"actions":["Turn a low pear upward so its stem releases without a jerk."],"consequences":["Fruit enters the basket; the tree stays whole."],"prose_obligations":["Describe care, not force."],"implemented_ids":["pick_fruit"],"implementation_note":"The scene records the available harvest and remaining fruit."},{"id":"gather_windfalls","role":"harvest encounter","location":"ground beneath tree","prerequisites":["Reaching the branches is unsafe or beyond reach."],"actions":["Check fallen pears for sound fruit and gather only those."],"consequences":["The friends can still carry a small snack without touching a branch."],"prose_obligations":["Do not claim windfalls exist beyond the validated parameter count."],"implemented_ids":["pick_fruit"],"implementation_note":"The windfalls parameter bounds the local action."},{"id":"leave_tree_unharmed","role":"physical consequence","location":"pear tree","prerequisites":["The friends finish gathering fruit."],"actions":["Leave leaves, limbs, and bark intact."],"consequences":["The orchard remains undamaged."],"prose_obligations":["Keep the physical result consistent in both endings."],"implemented_ids":["pick_fruit"],"implementation_note":"No separate no-op action is recorded; the harvest invariant validates this consequence."},{"id":"carry_fruit_to_snack","role":"useful return of borrowed object","location":"tree to picnic spot","prerequisites":["Fruit is in the basket."],"actions":["Carry the pears to the lunch cloth or stable crate."],"consequences":["The basket performs its useful purpose before being returned."],"prose_obligations":["Do not treat custody alone as repayment."],"implemented_ids":["share_snack"],"implementation_note":"Basket location and load change in the sharing scene."},{"id":"set_snack_surface","role":"optional payoff","location":"picnic spot","prerequisites":["The crate vignette may have established a level surface."],"actions":["Use the crate if level; otherwise use the cloth."],"consequences":["The snack surface reflects the optional vignette."],"prose_obligations":["An omitted crate scene must not secretly alter the surface."],"implemented_ids":["share_snack"],"implementation_note":"The persistent surface is read from state; the default is the cloth."},{"id":"divide_fruit","role":"emotional payoff","location":"picnic spot","prerequisites":["The harvest has been carried to the picnic spot."],"actions":["Cut each pear into equal halves and share it with the bread."],"consequences":["Both friends eat; a single pear is still enough for a shared snack."],"prose_obligations":["Resolve the want to share fairly, not just the harvest count."],"implemented_ids":["share_snack"],"implementation_note":"Consolidated with setting out bread and emptying the basket."},{"id":"abundant_snack_ending","role":"ending","location":"shed and orchard path","prerequisites":["At least two pears were gathered and shared."],"actions":["Walk back, clean, and return the basket."],"consequences":["The friends complete a shared harvest snack and leave the tree intact."],"prose_obligations":["Earn the fuller ending through accessible fruit and careful work."],"implemented_ids":["ending_full"],"implementation_note":"One of two mutually exclusive executable endings."},{"id":"one_pear_ending","role":"ending","location":"shed and orchard path","prerequisites":["Exactly one pear was gathered and shared."],"actions":["Walk back, clean, and return the basket."],"consequences":["A modest but complete snack ends the day without damaging the tree."],"prose_obligations":["Give the low-yield outcome emotional closure, not a deferred plan."],"implemented_ids":["ending_small"],"implementation_note":"One of two mutually exclusive executable endings."},{"id":"return_basket_clean","role":"closing encounter","location":"Ms. Vale's shed","prerequisites":["The basket has carried the fruit and is empty."],"actions":["Wipe the rim and return the borrowed basket."],"consequences":["Ms. Vale receives a useful, clean basket; borrowing has a completed payoff."],"prose_obligations":["Show both the basket's use and its return."],"implemented_ids":["ending_full","ending_small"],"implementation_note":"Consolidated into both ending scenes; no unselected ending effects execute."}]}"},{"path":"storyscenes/mini_adventures/kite/prose.py","content":"'''Scene-level prose for the orchard adventure; each paragraph follows enacted state.'''


def render(scene_id, before, after):
    if scene_id == 'borrow_basket':
        return ('Mira and Theo reached Ms. Vale’s shed with two slices of bread in Mira’s pocket and an empty lunch cloth. “Could we borrow the picking basket?” Mira asked. Ms. Vale passed it over. “Bring it back clean.” Theo lifted both handles. It would carry their pears while they kept their hands free for careful picking. They walked together into the orchard.')

    if scene_id == 'vignette_crate':
        if after['crate.used_as_table']:
            return ('At the orchard edge, Theo found a wooden crate and pressed one corner. It sat level. “A table, not a ladder,” he said. They spread the lunch cloth across it for sorting. Mira grinned. “Good. I wasn’t planning to climb anything.” The crate waited beside the path, ready to hold their bread.')
        return ('The crate at the orchard edge rocked when Theo tested it. “Not a step,” he said, nudging it aside. Mira spread their cloth on the grass instead. “There. A table that can’t tip.” He laughed, and they left the crate exactly where it was rather than making a risky perch of it.')

    if scene_id == 'vignette_memory':
        return ('While they walked, Mira remembered the pear they had split last summer, juice running down both wrists. “You gave me the bigger half,” Theo said. “You were smaller.” “I still am, according to the old gate.” Mira laughed. The memory made this snack feel like something they were choosing together, not a prize for one of them.')

    if scene_id == 'survey_tree':
        if after['tree.safe_reach']:
            return ('They stopped beneath the tree. The morning was still, and Mira could comfortably reach the lowest ripe pears without stretching onto her toes. Higher fruit stayed out of reach; neither friend considered tugging a limb. “We have enough down here,” Theo said. They looked for firm fruit, not a shortcut.')
        if after['tree.windy']:
            return ('They stopped beneath the tree as a gust set the narrow limbs moving. The ripe cluster bobbed above Mira’s comfortable reach. Theo looked at the shaking leaves, then at a pear resting on the grass. “No climbing, and no pulling,” he said. Mira agreed. “We can make a snack without asking the tree to take a risk.”')
        return ('They stopped beneath the tree. The lower ripe pears hung higher than Mira could comfortably reach, while one sound pear rested on the grass. Theo measured the distance with his eyes. “No climbing, and no pulling,” he said. Mira nodded. “We can make a snack without asking the tree to take a risk.”')

    if scene_id == 'choose_harvest':
        if after['harvest.plan'] == 'low_branch':
            return ('“Those low pears are reachable, but the high ones would mean stretching,” Mira said. Theo tapped the basket’s rim. “We pick what comes away gently and leave the rest.” Mira nodded. They chose the lower cluster, one pear at a time; no crate, shoulder, or branch would become a ladder. The choice cost them the tempting fruit above.')
        reason = 'The leaves are moving, and that cluster can wait.' if after['tree.windy'] else 'The ripe cluster is beyond a comfortable reach.'
        return (f'“Could we shake the branch?” Mira asked. {reason} “No,” Theo said, steady and plain. “The tree doesn’t owe us a snack.” They chose fallen fruit instead. Mira checked it gently for bruises. A smaller harvest was worth more to them than a damaged limb or a pear knocked down in a hurry.')

    if scene_id == 'pick_fruit':
        count = after['harvest.count']
        noun = 'pear' if count == 1 else 'pears'
        if after['harvest.source'] == 'low_branch':
            return (f'Mira turned each low pear upward, the way Ms. Vale had shown her; the stems let go without a jerk. Theo steadied the basket by its rim, not the branch. They gathered {count} ripe {noun}, leaving higher fruit and every leaf untouched. The tree stood just as it had before.')
        return (f'The friends checked the grass beneath the tree and found {count} sound fallen {noun}. Mira wiped away a speck of soil with the cloth; Theo placed them in the basket, not on the limbs above. They left the remaining fruit alone. Nothing was pulled, shaken, or broken.')

    if scene_id == 'share_snack':
        surface = 'the level crate' if after['picnic.surface'] == 'crate' else 'their lunch cloth'
        callback = ('Mira remembered their old picnic; this time Theo passed her an equal half.'
                    if after['friends.memory'] else 'They ate slowly, listening to the leaves.')
        return (f'On {surface}, Mira set out the bread while Theo lifted the fruit from the basket. They cut each pear into equal halves, so both friends received the same sweet share. The basket had carried the harvest safely; now it had done its useful work. {callback}')

    if scene_id == 'ending_full':
        return ('On the way back, they carried the empty basket between them. At the shed, Mira brushed away the leaves and Theo returned it to Ms. Vale. “It carried our snack beautifully,” Mira said. Vale checked the clean weave. “And you left my tree whole.” Their bread-and-pear lunch was finished; the afternoon felt shared.')

    if scene_id == 'ending_small':
        return ('On the way back, they carried the empty basket between them. At the shed, Theo brushed its rim clean and Mira returned it to Ms. Vale. Their single pear had made two bright, sticky halves, and both had eaten. “Small snack, no broken branch,” Theo said. Mira squeezed his hand. It tasted like enough.')

    raise ValueError(f'No prose for scene: {scene_id}')
